{title: O For a Thousand Tongues to Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: G}
{time: 3/2}
{tempo: 96}

Verse 1
O [G]for a thousand [D]tongues to [G]sing my [C]great Re[G]deemer's [D]praise,
the [G]glories of my [C]God and [G]King, the [C]triumphs [G]of [D]his [G]grace!

Verse 2
My [G]gracious Master and [D]my God, [G]Assist me [C]to proclaim, [D]To
spread [G]through all the [C]earth abroad [G]The [C]honors [G]of [D]Thy [G]name.

Verse 3
Jesus! [G]the name that [D]charms our [G]fears, That [C]bids our [D]sorrows
cease; [G]'Tis music in [C]the sinner's [G]ears, 'Tis life, [C]and [G]health, [D]and [G]peace.

Verse 4
He [G]breaks the pow'r [D]of canceled [G]sin, He [C]sets the [D]prisoner
free; [G]His blood can [C]make the [G]foulest clean, His [C]blood [G]availed [D]for [G]me.

Verse 5
He [G]speaks, and, listening [D]to [G]His voice, [C]New life [D]the
dead [G]receive, The mournful, [C]broken hearts [G]rejoice, [C]The [G]humble [D]poor [G]believe.
